---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/guides/email-sms-coordination';
const title = 'Email + SMS Campaign Coordination | Shopify SMS Marketing';
const desc = 'Give each channel a job, record the combined customer journey, and check eligibility again before a delayed message leaves the queue.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} dateModified="2026-11-25" />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/guides" class="link text-sm">← All SMS guides</a>
      <p class="badge mt-6">Plan one customer journey</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Email + SMS Campaign Coordination</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-orange-950/80">{desc}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
<h2>Start with the message job</h2>
<p>Email has room for product education, comparisons and a maker story. SMS can carry a concise access link or a time-sensitive reminder. These are useful design choices, not permanent assignments to particular vendors. A bundled platform may simplify profile management; separate tools may suit teams with different channel needs. Either arrangement needs an explicit owner for shared exclusions and the send calendar.</p>
<p>For a proposed limited-release campaign, put the product explanation in email and reserve a text for subscribers who requested release access. Do not assume every email recipient is eligible for SMS. A subscriber with both permissions may need only one reminder; someone who already purchased needs a different next step.</p>
<h2>Write a campaign handoff record</h2>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>What to record</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Purpose and owner</td><td>Release access, campaign identifier, approver and person who can cancel both channels</td></tr>
<tr><td>Audience</td><td>Permission per channel, product interest, market and exclusions</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sequence</td><td>First message, follow-up condition, expiry and destination time handling</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shared state</td><td>Purchase, opt-out, subscription status and last relevant message</td></tr>
<tr><td>Failure action</td><td>Who pauses the queue when stock, consent data or an integration is stale</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Keep the offer, eligible products and deadline consistent between the landing page and both messages. If email offers a bundle and SMS announces access, say which audience gets which benefit. Avoid making subscribers search both channels to understand the actual price.</p>
<h2>Frequency settings may stop at the channel boundary</h2>
<p><a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002779311">Klaviyo documents separate Smart Sending windows for email, SMS and push</a>. Enabling a window does not itself establish a combined contact limit. This is a scoped product example, checked November 25, 2026; inspect your actual campaign and flow settings rather than assuming every tool behaves alike.</p>
<p>Choose spacing around the customer's task and the offer deadline. A fixed twelve-hour gap can be too late for a short release and unnecessary for a requested alert. Record the chosen interval, which automated messages can still run, and whether skipped messages are discarded or rescheduled. Distinguish marketing from service messages before applying exclusions.</p>
<h2>Rehearse four paths before launch</h2>
<ol><li>Email permission only: confirm the profile never enters the SMS audience.</li><li>Both permissions: inspect the entire sequence, including existing welcome and cart flows.</li><li>Purchase after the first message: confirm the promotional follow-up rechecks the order event before dispatch.</li><li>Opt-out while queued: confirm suppression reaches the sending system and the queued message cannot bypass it.</li></ol>
<p>These are proposed checks, not tests we performed. Use controlled profiles and retain expected versus actual timestamps. Test a delayed event and a duplicate profile too: matching by email alone can leave a phone-based record outside the purchase exclusion. If one channel cannot receive an exclusion reliably, pause its overlapping campaign while the mapping is repaired.</p>
<h2>Handle inventory and deadlines as shared inputs</h2>
<p>A delayed text should not announce stock that has sold out. Assign someone to update the landing page and cancel obsolete reminders. For waitlists, define whether access is first come, reserved, or drawn; an early link does not reserve a unit. Do not turn a stock estimate into a scarcity claim without checking the inventory source and update lag.</p>
<p>For subscription products, decide whether an active subscriber should receive the release announcement, a renewal-specific message or no promotion. A purchase exclusion for one SKU need not suppress unrelated requested information. Document the decision instead of applying a blanket all-channel exit.</p>
<h2>Evaluate the combined journey</h2>
<p>Review delivered messages, purchases, opt-outs, support replies and costs by campaign identifier. Platform-attributed revenue can overlap across channels. If the question is whether the extra SMS adds value, compare an eligible email-only group with a randomized eligible email-plus-SMS group, keeping the offer and observation window consistent. Small samples or cross-channel exposure can leave the result inconclusive.</p>
<p>Use <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> to decide which follow-up deserves a slot, <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a> to compare incentives, and <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">consent records</a> to define channel eligibility. Buying another sender will not resolve an unowned handoff.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
